# Options of the XiaoTai settings module. Each maps to the macro of the same
# name without the CONFIG_ prefix in
# include/xiaotai/modules/settings_config.h; the defaults here and there are
# the same.
menu "XiaoTai settings module"

    config XIAOTAI_SETTINGS_TAKE_BACK_LATE_REFUSAL
        bool "Take a setting back when the audio hardware refuses it later"
        default n
        help
            When the media engine reports that it could not apply a volume,
            speaker mute or microphone gain the user changed, the setting
            returns to the value the hardware still has and the application
            hears settings.refused. Off: the setting and the stored
            preference keep the user's value; the failure is only counted.
            Refusals the engine returns at once are taken back either way.

    config XIAOTAI_SETTINGS_VOLUME_UP_UNMUTES
        bool "Raising the volume with a step clears the speaker mute"
        default n
        help
            A volume step upwards (keys, voice command, intent
            audio.volume_up) also unmutes the speaker. Off: the mute stays.

endmenu
